Co, Inc. engages in the manufacture, marketing, distribution, and sale of various beverages and convenient foods worldwide. The company operates through six segments: PepsiCo Foods North America; PepsiCo Beverages North America; International Beverages Franchise; Europe, Middle East and Africa; Latin America Foods; and Asia Pacific Foods. It offers cereals, chips, dips, granola bars, oatmeal, pasta, rice, and syrups and mixes; refrigerated dips and spreads; beverage concentrates, fountain syrups, and finished goods; and ready-to-drink tea and coffee products. The company also provides SodaStream sparkling water makers and related products, as well as various dairy products under the Agusha, Chudo, and Domik v Derevne brands. It serves wholesale and other distributors, foodservice customers, grocery stores, drug stores, convenience stores, discount/dollar stores, mass merchandisers, membership stores, hard discounters, e-commerce retailers and authorized independent bottlers, and others through a network of direct-store-delivery, customer warehouse, and distributor networks, as well as directly to consumers through e-commerce platforms and retailers. PepsiCo, Inc. was founded in 1898 and is based in Purchase, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ramon Luis Laguarta | Chairman & CEO | Age 61 | Compensation: $8.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 306K people. Revenue per employee of $307K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $25K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $941 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 27\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Pepsico, Inc. is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $192.6B market cap on $93.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 6% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 55% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $7.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 10.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Large open-market insider purchases (net $18.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","53 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PepsiCo (PEP) Could Be 29% Undervalued Following Its KFC Deal Renewal","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/pepsico-pep-could-29-undervalued-191920390.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PepsiCo Quietly Closed 3 Frito-Lay Factories: Are More To Come?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/frito-lay-quietly-closing-factories-090000000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794005924.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"If You Invested $1,000 in PepsiCo 10 Years Ago, Here\u2019s What You\u2019d Have Now","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/invested-1-000-pepsico-10-191735966.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992655.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Celsius Holdings (CELH) Stock Rallies As Q3 Earnings Spotlight Margin Risks","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/celsius-holdings-celh-stock-rallies-011228737.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013948.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Celsius Holding